IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap1-logic`

-- 7 U.S.C. 2018: approval of retail food stores and wholesale food concerns.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text).
-- Seams taken as inputs, named for the answering section: s 2012(k) (three inputs), s 2016(h)(3)(B), s 2020(e)(25), s 2021(a).
-- ANSWERS this module gives the family: `s 2018(h) permitted under section 2018(h)` (BOOLEAN; the keel's three fields of s 2012(k) ask it).
-- Duties with a deadline (subsection (h)(3) and (i)(1)(D)) have a regulative rule, whose outcome is printed by #TRACE in the tests (a DEONTIC value cannot be
-- compared by #ASSERT on the stable binary), and a decision function that is asserted.

§ `s 2018(a) Authorization to accept and redeem benefits`

-- src:1345 | Regulations issued pursuant to this chapter shall provide for the submission of applications for approval by retail food stores and wholesale food concerns which desire to be authorized to accept and redeem benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and for the approval of those applicants whose participation will effectuate the purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2018(a)(1)(A) (src:1345)
GIVEN `the applicant's participation will effectuate the purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(a)(1)(A) the applicant is to be approved under the regulations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the applicant's participation will effectuate the purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Regulations ... shall provide ... for the approval of those applicants whose participation will effectuate the purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the regulations are to provide for "the approval of those applicants whose participation will effectuate the purposes"

DECLARE `s 2018(a)(1)(B) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(i) the nature and extent of the food business conducted by the applicant`
    `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(ii) the volume of benefit transactions which may reasonably be expected to be conducted by the applicant food store or wholesale food concern`
    `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(iii) whether the applicant is located in an area with significantly limited access to food`
    `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(iv) any information, if available, about the ability of the anticipated or existing electronic benefit transfer equipment and service provider of the applicant to provide sufficient information through the electronic benefit transfer system to minimize the risk of fraudulent transactions`
    `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(v) the business integrity and reputation of the applicant`

-- src:1347 | In determining the qualifications of applicants, there shall be considered among such other factors as may be appropriate, the following:
-- src:1348 | (i) the nature and extent of the food business conducted by the applicant;
-- src:1349 | (ii) the volume of benefit transactions which may reasonably be expected to be conducted by the applicant food store or wholesale food concern;
-- src:1350 | (iii) whether the applicant is located in an area with significantly limited access to food;
-- src:1351 | (iv) any information, if available, about the ability of the anticipated or existing electronic benefit transfer equipment and service provider of the applicant to provide sufficient information through the electronic benefit transfer system to minimize the risk of fraudulent transactions; and
-- src:1352 | (v) the business integrity and reputation of the applicant.
@ref s 2018(a)(1)(B), the factors (src:1347-1352)
`s 2018(a)(1)(B) the factors that must be considered among such other factors as may be appropriate` MEANS
    LIST `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(i) the nature and extent of the food business conducted by the applicant`
       , `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(ii) the volume of benefit transactions which may reasonably be expected to be conducted by the applicant food store or wholesale food concern`
       , `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(iii) whether the applicant is located in an area with significantly limited access to food`
       , `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(iv) any information, if available, about the ability of the anticipated or existing electronic benefit transfer equipment and service provider of the applicant to provide sufficient information through the electronic benefit transfer system to minimize the risk of fraudulent transactions`
       , `s 2018(a)(1)(B)(v) the business integrity and reputation of the applicant`

-- src:1354 | Approval of an applicant shall be evidenced by the issuance to such applicant of a nontransferable certificate of approval.
@ref s 2018(a)(1)(C), evidence of approval (src:1354)
GIVEN `the applicant has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(a)(1)(C) the approval is evidenced by the issuance of a certificate of approval` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the applicant has been approved`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Approval of an applicant shall be evidenced by the issuance to such applicant of a nontransferable certificate of approval"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for the "approval of an applicant"

-- src:1354 | Approval of an applicant shall be evidenced by the issuance to such applicant of a nontransferable certificate of approval.
@ref s 2018(a)(1)(C), nontransferable (src:1354)
GIVEN `the certificate is the certificate of approval issued to the approved applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(a)(1)(C) the certificate of approval may be transferred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the certificate is the certificate of approval issued to the approved applicant`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a nontransferable certificate of approval"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the word "nontransferable" is of the "certificate of approval" that evidences approval

-- src:1356 | No retail food store or wholesale food concern of a type determined by the Secretary, based on factors that include size, location, and type of items sold, shall be approved to be authorized or reauthorized for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless an authorized employee of the Department of Agriculture, a designee of the Secretary, or, if practicable, an official of the State or local government designated by the Secretary has visited the store or concern for the purpose of determining whether the store or concern should be approved or reauthorized, as appropriate.
@ref s 2018(a)(1)(D), visit required (src:1356)
GIVEN `the store or concern is of a type determined by the Secretary, based on factors that include size, location, and type of items sold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorized employee of the Department of Agriculture, a designee of the Secretary, or, if practicable, an official of the State or local government designated by the Secretary has visited the store or concern for the purpose of determining whether it should be approved or reauthorized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(a)(1)(D) the store or concern may be approved to be authorized or reauthorized` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the store or concern is of a type determined by the Secretary, based on factors that include size, location, and type of items sold`
           AND NOT `an authorized employee of the Department of Agriculture, a designee of the Secretary, or, if practicable, an official of the State or local government designated by the Secretary has visited the store or concern for the purpose of determining whether it should be approved or reauthorized`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No retail food store or wholesale food concern of a type determined by the Secretary ... shall be approved to be authorized or reauthorized for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless an authorized employee of the Department of Agriculture ... has visited the store or concern"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "unless" a visit has been made, and a visit does not itself approve the store or concern

§ `s 2018(b) Effective and efficient operation of program; effect of disqualification`

-- src:1365 | (1) No wholesale food concern may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits unless the Secretary determines that its participation is required for the effective and efficient operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program. No co-located wholesale-retail food concern may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as a retail food store, unless (A) the concern does a substantial level of retail food business, or (B) the Secretary determines that failure to authorize such a food concern as a retail food store would cause hardship to households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits. In addition, no firm may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as both a retail food store and as a wholesale food concern at the same time.
@ref s 2018(b)(1), first sentence (src:1365)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines that the participation of the wholesale food concern is required for the effective and efficient operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(b)(1) the wholesale food concern may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Secretary determines that the participation of the wholesale food concern is required for the effective and efficient operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No wholesale food concern may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits unless the Secretary determines that its participation is required for the effective and efficient operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "unless" the Secretary so determines, and the determination does not itself authorize the concern

-- src:1365 | No co-located wholesale-retail food concern may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as a retail food store, unless (A) the concern does a substantial level of retail food business, or (B) the Secretary determines that failure to authorize such a food concern as a retail food store would cause hardship to households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits.
@ref s 2018(b)(1), second sentence (src:1365)
GIVEN `the concern does a substantial level of retail food business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that failure to authorize the concern as a retail food store would cause hardship to households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(b)(1) the co-located wholesale-retail food concern may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as a retail food store` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the concern does a substantial level of retail food business` OR `the Secretary determines that failure to authorize the concern as a retail food store would cause hardship to households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No co-located wholesale-retail food concern may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as a retail food store, unless (A) the concern does a substantial level of retail food business, or (B) the Secretary determines that failure to authorize such a food concern as a retail food store would cause hardship"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "unless" one of two conditions holds, and either does not itself authorize the concern

-- src:1365 | (1) No wholesale food concern may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits unless the Secretary determines that its participation is required for the effective and efficient operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program. No co-located wholesale-retail food concern may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as a retail food store, unless (A) the concern does a substantial level of retail food business, or (B) the Secretary determines that failure to authorize such a food concern as a retail food store would cause hardship to households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits. In addition, no firm may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as both a retail food store and as a wholesale food concern at the same time.
@ref s 2018(b)(1), third sentence (src:1365)
GIVEN `the firm would be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as both a retail food store and a wholesale food concern at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(b)(1) the firm may be authorized as both a retail food store and a wholesale food concern at the same time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the firm would be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as both a retail food store and a wholesale food concern at the same time`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no firm may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits as both a retail food store and as a wholesale food concern at the same time"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on authorization "as both ... at the same time"

-- src:1367 | (A) A buyer or transferee (other than a bona fide buyer or transferee) of a retail food store or wholesale food concern that has been disqualified under section 2021(a) of this title may not accept or redeem benefits until the Secretary receives full payment of any penalty imposed on such store or concern.
@ref s 2018(b)(2)(A) (src:1367)
GIVEN `s 2021(a) the retail food store or wholesale food concern has been disqualified under section 2021(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer or transferee is a bona fide buyer or transferee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has received full payment of any penalty imposed on the store or concern` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(b)(2)(A) the buyer or transferee may accept or redeem benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2021(a) the retail food store or wholesale food concern has been disqualified under section 2021(a)` AND (NOT `the buyer or transferee is a bona fide buyer or transferee`) AND (NOT `the Secretary has received full payment of any penalty imposed on the store or concern`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A buyer or transferee (other than a bona fide buyer or transferee) of a retail food store or wholesale food concern that has been disqualified under section 2021(a) of this title may not accept or redeem benefits until the Secretary receives full payment of any penalty"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a buyer or transferee "(other than a bona fide buyer or transferee)" of a disqualified store or concern, and "until" the Secretary receives full payment

-- src:1368 | (B) A buyer or transferee may not, as a result of the sale or transfer of such store or concern, be required to furnish a bond under section 2021(d) of this title.
@ref s 2018(b)(2)(B) (src:1368)
GIVEN `the requirement to furnish a bond under section 2021(d) is imposed as a result of the sale or transfer of the store or concern` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(b)(2)(B) the buyer or transferee may be required to furnish a bond under section 2021(d)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirement to furnish a bond under section 2021(d) is imposed as a result of the sale or transfer of the store or concern`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A buyer or transferee may not, as a result of the sale or transfer of such store or concern, be required to furnish a bond under section 2021(d)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a requirement imposed "as a result of the sale or transfer"

§ `s 2018(c) Information submitted by applicants`

DECLARE `s 2018(c) penalty` HAS
    `s 2018(c) the greatest fine, in dollars`        IS A NUMBER
    `s 2018(c) the longest imprisonment, in years`   IS A NUMBER

-- src:1370 | such information may be disclosed to and used by Federal law enforcement and investigative agencies and law enforcement and investigative agencies of a State government for the purposes of administering or enforcing this chapter or any other Federal or State law and the regulations issued under this chapter or such law, and State agencies that administer the special supplemental nutrition program for women, infants and children, authorized under section 17 of the Child Nutrition Act of 1966 [42 U.S.C. 1786], for purposes of administering the provisions of that Act [42 U.S.C. 1771 et seq.] and the regulations issued under that Act.
@ref s 2018(c), the disclosure that is authorized (src:1370)
GIVEN `the recipient is a Federal law enforcement or investigative agency, or a law enforcement or investigative agency of a State government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is administering or enforcing this chapter or any other Federal or State law and the regulations issued under this chapter or such law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is a State agency that administers the special supplemental nutrition program for women, infants and children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is administering the provisions of the Child Nutrition Act of 1966 and the regulations issued under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(c) the information obtained under the subsection may be disclosed to and used by the recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the recipient is a Federal law enforcement or investigative agency, or a law enforcement or investigative agency of a State government` AND `the purpose is administering or enforcing this chapter or any other Federal or State law and the regulations issued under this chapter or such law`)
           OR (`the recipient is a State agency that administers the special supplemental nutrition program for women, infants and children` AND `the purpose is administering the provisions of the Child Nutrition Act of 1966 and the regulations issued under that Act`)
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "such information may be disclosed to and used by Federal law enforcement and investigative agencies and law enforcement and investigative agencies of a State government for the purposes of administering or enforcing this chapter or any other Federal or State law"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception names its recipients and purposes, and the safeguards limit use "to purposes directly connected with administration and enforcement" of the chapter and its regulations

-- src:1370 | Regulations issued pursuant to this chapter shall require an applicant retail food store or wholesale food concern to submit information, which may include relevant income and sales tax filing documents, purchase invoices, records relating to electronic benefit transfer equipment and related services, transaction and redemption data provided through the electronic benefit transfer system, or program-related records, which will permit a determination to be made as to whether such applicant qualifies, or continues to qualify, for approval under the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter. The regulations may require retail food stores and wholesale food concerns to provide written authorization for the Secretary to verify all relevant tax filings with appropriate agencies and to obtain corroborating documentation from other sources so that the accuracy of information provided by the stores and concerns may be verified. Regulations issued pursuant to this chapter shall provide for safeguards which limit the use or disclosure of information obtained under the authority granted by this subsection to purposes directly connected with administration and enforcement of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter, except that such information may be disclosed to and used by Federal law enforcement and investigative agencies and law enforcement and investigative agencies of a State government for the purposes of administering or enforcing this chapter or any other Federal or State law and the regulations issued under this chapter or such law, and State agencies that administer the special supplemental nutrition program for women, infants and children, authorized under section 17 of the Child Nutrition Act of 1966 [42 U.S.C. 1786], for purposes of administering the provisions of that Act [42 U.S.C. 1771 et seq.] and the regulations issued under that Act. Any person who publishes, divulges, discloses, or makes known in any manner or to any extent not authorized by Federal law (including a regulation) any information obtained under this subsection shall be fined not more than $1,000 or imprisoned not more than 1 year, or both. The regulations shall establish the criteria to be used by the Secretary to determine whether the information is needed. The regulations shall not prohibit the audit and examination of such information by the Comptroller General of the United States authorized by any other provision of law.
@ref s 2018(c), the offence and its penalty (src:1370)
GIVEN `the person publishes, divulges, discloses, or makes known any information obtained under the subsection in a manner or to an extent not authorized by Federal law (including a regulation)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 2018(c) penalty`
`s 2018(c) the penalty to which the person is liable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person publishes, divulges, discloses, or makes known any information obtained under the subsection in a manner or to an extent not authorized by Federal law (including a regulation)`
            THEN JUST (`s 2018(c) penalty` WITH
                    `s 2018(c) the greatest fine, in dollars` IS 1000
                    `s 2018(c) the longest imprisonment, in years` IS 1)  -- the text says yes: "shall be fined not more than $1,000 or imprisoned not more than 1 year, or both"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is for a disclosure "in any manner or to any extent not authorized by Federal law (including a regulation)"

-- src:1370 | Regulations issued pursuant to this chapter shall require an applicant retail food store or wholesale food concern to submit information, which may include relevant income and sales tax filing documents, purchase invoices, records relating to electronic benefit transfer equipment and related services, transaction and redemption data provided through the electronic benefit transfer system, or program-related records, which will permit a determination to be made as to whether such applicant qualifies, or continues to qualify, for approval under the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter. The regulations may require retail food stores and wholesale food concerns to provide written authorization for the Secretary to verify all relevant tax filings with appropriate agencies and to obtain corroborating documentation from other sources so that the accuracy of information provided by the stores and concerns may be verified. Regulations issued pursuant to this chapter shall provide for safeguards which limit the use or disclosure of information obtained under the authority granted by this subsection to purposes directly connected with administration and enforcement of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter, except that such information may be disclosed to and used by Federal law enforcement and investigative agencies and law enforcement and investigative agencies of a State government for the purposes of administering or enforcing this chapter or any other Federal or State law and the regulations issued under this chapter or such law, and State agencies that administer the special supplemental nutrition program for women, infants and children, authorized under section 17 of the Child Nutrition Act of 1966 [42 U.S.C. 1786], for purposes of administering the provisions of that Act [42 U.S.C. 1771 et seq.] and the regulations issued under that Act. Any person who publishes, divulges, discloses, or makes known in any manner or to any extent not authorized by Federal law (including a regulation) any information obtained under this subsection shall be fined not more than $1,000 or imprisoned not more than 1 year, or both. The regulations shall establish the criteria to be used by the Secretary to determine whether the information is needed. The regulations shall not prohibit the audit and examination of such information by the Comptroller General of the United States authorized by any other provision of law.
@ref s 2018(c), the limits of the penalty (src:1370)
GIVEN `the fine imposed, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the imprisonment imposed, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(c) the sentence is within the limits the subsection sets` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the fine imposed, in dollars` GREATER THAN 1000 OR `the imprisonment imposed, in years` GREATER THAN 1
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be fined not more than $1,000 or imprisoned not more than 1 year, or both"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall be fined not more than $1,000 or imprisoned not more than 1 year, or both" (assumed, not ruled: the function is named for the limits, so a fine of at most $1,000 and a term of at most 1 year is within them; the other way, reading (b) of a ceiling, is OTHERWISE NOTHING with the two assertions at the head of the s 2018(c) tests set to NOTHING)

§ `s 2018(d) Hearing and waiting period`

-- src:1372 | Any retail food store or wholesale food concern which has failed upon application to receive approval to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program may obtain a hearing on such refusal as provided in section 2023 of this title. A retail food store or wholesale food concern that is denied approval to accept and redeem benefits because the store or concern does not meet criteria for approval established by the Secretary may not, for at least 6 months, submit a new application to participate in the program. The Secretary may establish a longer time period under the preceding sentence, including permanent disqualification, that reflects the severity of the basis of the denial.
@ref s 2018(d), first sentence (src:1372)
GIVEN `the retail food store or wholesale food concern has failed upon application to receive approval to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(d) the store or concern may obtain a hearing on the refusal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the retail food store or wholesale food concern has failed upon application to receive approval to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "may obtain a hearing on such refusal as provided in section 2023"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for a store or concern "which has failed upon application to receive approval"

-- The waiting period is six months at least, and any longer period the Secretary sets (an input of the core's type, so that "permanently" is one of its values).
-- src:1372 | A retail food store or wholesale food concern that is denied approval to accept and redeem benefits because the store or concern does not meet criteria for approval established by the Secretary may not, for at least 6 months, submit a new application to participate in the program. The Secretary may establish a longer time period under the preceding sentence, including permanent disqualification, that reflects the severity of the basis of the denial.
@ref s 2018(d), second and third sentences (src:1372)
GIVEN `the store or concern was denied approval because it does not meet criteria for approval established by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the denial` IS A DATE
      `the date of the new application` IS A DATE
      `the longer period the Secretary has established, if any` IS A MAYBE `Period of ineligibility`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(d) the store or concern may submit a new application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the store or concern was denied approval because it does not meet criteria for approval established by the Secretary`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the waiting period is for a store or concern "denied approval ... because the store or concern does not meet criteria for approval established by the Secretary"
        IF `the date of the new application` LESS THAN `the date of the denial`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the new application is dated before the denial
        IF `snap1 whole months from the earlier date to the later date` `the date of the denial` `the date of the new application` LESS THAN 6
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not, for at least 6 months, submit a new application to participate in the program"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the longer period the Secretary has established, if any`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "for at least 6 months" and no longer period was supplied
                WHEN JUST period THEN `s 2018(d) the longer period bars the new application` period (`snap1 whole months from the earlier date to the later date` `the date of the denial` `the date of the new application`)

-- src:1372 | Any retail food store or wholesale food concern which has failed upon application to receive approval to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program may obtain a hearing on such refusal as provided in section 2023 of this title. A retail food store or wholesale food concern that is denied approval to accept and redeem benefits because the store or concern does not meet criteria for approval established by the Secretary may not, for at least 6 months, submit a new application to participate in the program. The Secretary may establish a longer time period under the preceding sentence, including permanent disqualification, that reflects the severity of the basis of the denial.
@ref s 2018(d), third sentence (src:1372)
GIVEN period IS A `Period of ineligibility`
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(d) the longer period bars the new application` MEANS
    CONSIDER period
        WHEN `for a number of months` m THEN (IF months LESS THAN m THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may establish a longer time period under the preceding sentence"; NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the longer period has run
        WHEN `for a number of years` y THEN (IF months LESS THAN (y TIMES 12) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may establish a longer time period under the preceding sentence"; NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the longer period has run
        WHEN `permanently` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "including permanent disqualification"
        WHEN `for a number of days` d THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a longer period counted in days is not converted into months here
        WHEN `until a stated condition ends` c THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a period that ends with a condition is not decided by dates
        WHEN `for a period the Secretary prescribes by regulation, not stated in this text` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the length is the Secretary's
        WHEN `for a period the State agency determines, not stated in this text` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the length is not the Secretary's to set in this sentence

§ `s 2018(e) to (g) Sign, house-to-house trade routes, EBT service`

-- src:1374 | Approved retail food stores shall display a sign providing information on how persons may report abuses they have observed in the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2018(e) (src:1374)
GIVEN `the retail food store is an approved retail food store` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the store displays a sign providing information on how persons may report abuses they have observed in the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(e) the approved retail food store has not displayed the sign` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the retail food store is an approved retail food store`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is on "approved retail food stores"
        IF `the store displays a sign providing information on how persons may report abuses they have observed in the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the store has done what "Approved retail food stores shall display a sign providing information on how persons may report abuses" requires
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Approved retail food stores shall display a sign"

-- src:1376 | In those areas in which the Secretary, in consultation with the Inspector General of the Department of Agriculture, finds evidence that the operation of house-to-house trade routes damages the program’s integrity, the Secretary shall limit the participation of house-to-house trade routes to those routes that are reasonably necessary to provide adequate access to households.
@ref s 2018(f) (src:1376)
GIVEN `the Secretary, in consultation with the Inspector General of the Department of Agriculture, finds evidence in the area that the operation of house-to-house trade routes damages the integrity of the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the route is reasonably necessary to provide adequate access to households` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(f) the house-to-house trade route may participate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Secretary, in consultation with the Inspector General of the Department of Agriculture, finds evidence in the area that the operation of house-to-house trade routes damages the integrity of the program`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the limit is "in those areas in which the Secretary ... finds evidence that the operation of house-to-house trade routes damages the program's integrity"
        IF NOT `the route is reasonably necessary to provide adequate access to households`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary shall limit the participation of house-to-house trade routes to those routes that are reasonably necessary to provide adequate access to households"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a limit "to those routes that are reasonably necessary" names who is outside; it does not say that those inside may participate

-- src:1378 | An approved retail food store shall provide adequate EBT service as described in section 2016(h)(3)(B) of this title.
@ref s 2018(g) (src:1378)
GIVEN `the retail food store is an approved retail food store` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2016(h)(3)(B) the EBT service the store provides is adequate EBT service as described in section 2016(h)(3)(B)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(g) the approved retail food store has not provided the adequate EBT service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the retail food store is an approved retail food store`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is on "an approved retail food store"
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2016(h)(3)(B) the EBT service the store provides is adequate EBT service as described in section 2016(h)(3)(B)`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the store has done what "An approved retail food store shall provide adequate EBT service" requires
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2016(h)(3)(B) the EBT service the store provides is adequate EBT service as described in section 2016(h)(3)(B)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "An approved retail food store shall provide adequate EBT service as described in section 2016(h)(3)(B)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the service is adequate EBT service as described in section 2016(h)(3)(B) was not supplied

§ `s 2018(h) Private establishments`

-- src:1384 | If, on the day before February 7, 2014, a State has entered into a contract with a private establishment described in paragraph (1) and the Secretary has not determined that the participation of the private establishment is necessary to meet a documented need in accordance with section 2020(e)(25) of this title, the Secretary shall allow the operation of the private establishment to continue without that determination of need for a period not to exceed 180 days from the date on which the Secretary establishes determination criteria, by regulation, under section 2020(e)(25) of this title.
@ref s 2018(h)(2)(A) (src:1384)
GIVEN `on the day before February 7, 2014, a State had entered into a contract with the private establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has not determined that the participation of the private establishment is necessary to meet a documented need` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the Secretary establishes determination criteria, by regulation, under section 2020(e)(25)` IS A DATE
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(h)(2)(A) the operation of the private establishment may continue without the determination of need` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`on the day before February 7, 2014, a State had entered into a contract with the private establishment` AND `the Secretary has not determined that the participation of the private establishment is necessary to meet a documented need`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, on the day before February 7, 2014, a State has entered into a contract with a private establishment described in paragraph (1) and the Secretary has not determined that the participation of the private establishment is necessary to meet a documented need ..., the Secretary shall allow the operation of the private establishment to continue" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        IF (Day `the date`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the Secretary establishes determination criteria, by regulation, under section 2020(e)(25)`) AT MOST 180
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "the Secretary shall allow the operation of the private establishment to continue without that determination of need for a period not to exceed 180 days from the date on which the Secretary establishes determination criteria"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the continuation is "for a period not to exceed 180 days from the date on which the Secretary establishes determination criteria"

-- src:1381 | Subject to paragraph (2), no private establishment that contracts with a State agency to offer meals at concessional prices as described in paragraphs (3), (4), and (9) of section 2012(k) of this title may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits unless the Secretary determines that the participation of the private establishment is required to meet a documented need in accordance with section 2020(e)(25) of this title.
@ref s 2018(h)(1) (src:1381)
GIVEN `s 2012(k) the establishment is one described in paragraphs (3), (4) and (9) of section 2012(k)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2020(e)(25) the Secretary determines that the participation of the private establishment is required to meet a documented need` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2018(h)(2)(A) the operation of the private establishment may continue without the determination of need` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(h)(1) the private establishment may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 2012(k) the establishment is one described in paragraphs (3), (4) and (9) of section 2012(k)`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is for a private establishment "that contracts with a State agency to offer meals at concessional prices as described in paragraphs (3), (4), and (9) of section 2012(k)"
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2018(h)(2)(A) the operation of the private establishment may continue without the determination of need`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Subject to paragraph (2)", where the Secretary "shall allow the operation of the private establishment to continue without that determination of need"
        IF NOT `s 2020(e)(25) the Secretary determines that the participation of the private establishment is required to meet a documented need`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no private establishment ... may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits unless the Secretary determines that the participation of the private establishment is required to meet a documented need"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "unless" the Secretary so determines, and the determination does not itself authorize the establishment

-- The keel's three fields of s 2012(k) (clauses (3), (4), (9)) ask whether the meals are "permitted under section 2018(h)". The keel types the field BOOLEAN, so the answer is TRUE
-- unless the text says no (a lossy step the keel asked for: NOTHING becomes TRUE here, never FALSE).
-- src:1381 | Subject to paragraph (2), no private establishment that contracts with a State agency to offer meals at concessional prices as described in paragraphs (3), (4), and (9) of section 2012(k) of this title may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits unless the Secretary determines that the participation of the private establishment is required to meet a documented need in accordance with section 2020(e)(25) of this title.
@ref s 2018(h), the answer the keel asks for (src:1381)
GIVEN `s 2020(e)(25) the Secretary determines that the participation of the private establishment is required to meet a documented need` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2018(h)(2)(A) the operation of the private establishment may continue without the determination of need` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2018(h) permitted under section 2018(h)` MEANS
    NOT (`snap1 is definitely no` (`s 2018(h)(1) the private establishment may be authorized to accept and redeem benefits` TRUE `s 2020(e)(25) the Secretary determines that the participation of the private establishment is required to meet a documented need` `s 2018(h)(2)(A) the operation of the private establishment may continue without the determination of need`))

-- src:1386 | If the Secretary determines to terminate a contract with a private establishment that is in effect on February 7, 2014, the Secretary shall provide justification to the State in which the private establishment is located for that termination.
@ref s 2018(h)(2)(B) (src:1386)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines to terminate a contract with a private establishment that is in effect on February 7, 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(h)(2)(B) the Secretary must provide justification to the State for the termination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary determines to terminate a contract with a private establishment that is in effect on February 7, 2014`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "the Secretary shall provide justification to the State in which the private establishment is located for that termination"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Secretary determines to terminate a contract with a private establishment that is in effect on February 7, 2014, the Secretary shall provide justification" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- (h)(3): the Secretary's report is due 90 days after the last day of each fiscal year, the first being 90 days after 30 September 2014. The last day of a fiscal year is 30 September.
-- src:1388 | Not later than 90 days after September 30, 2014, and 90 days after the last day of each fiscal year thereafter, the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report on the effectiveness of a program under this subsection using any information received from States under section 2020(e)(25) of this title as well as any other information the Secretary may have relating to the manner in which benefits are used.
@ref s 2018(h)(3), the date the report is due (src:1388)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2018(h)(3) the date the report is due` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the fiscal year` LESS THAN 2014
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the first report is due "90 days after September 30, 2014"
        OTHERWISE JUST (Date ((Day (Date 30 9 `the fiscal year`)) PLUS 90))  -- "90 days after the last day of each fiscal year thereafter"

-- src:1388 | Not later than 90 days after September 30, 2014, and 90 days after the last day of each fiscal year thereafter, the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report on the effectiveness of a program under this subsection using any information received from States under section 2020(e)(25) of this title as well as any other information the Secretary may have relating to the manner in which benefits are used.
@ref s 2018(h)(3), the report was in time (src:1388)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the report was submitted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(h)(3) the report was submitted not later than the date it was due` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2018(h)(3) the date the report is due` `the fiscal year`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the first report is due "90 days after September 30, 2014"
        WHEN JUST due THEN
            BRANCH
                IF `the date the report was submitted` AT MOST due
                    THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Not later than 90 days after ... the last day of each fiscal year"
                OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 90 days after September 30, 2014, and 90 days after the last day of each fiscal year thereafter, the Secretary shall submit"

DECLARE `s 2018(h)(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2018(h)(3) submit the report to the committees`

-- Time is counted in days from the last day of the fiscal year.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 2018(h)(3) act`
`s 2018(h)(3) the duty to submit the report` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2018(h)(3) submit the report to the committees`
    WITHIN 90
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the report on the effectiveness of a program under subsection (h) was not submitted within 90 days after the last day of the fiscal year"

§ `s 2018(i) Review of program operations`

-- src:1392 | (A) shall review a representative sample of currently authorized facilities referred to in section 2012(k)(3) of this title to determine whether benefits are properly used by or on behalf of participating households residing in such facilities and whether such facilities are using more than 1 source of Federal or State funding to meet the food needs of residents;
@ref s 2018(i)(1)(A) (src:1392)
GIVEN `s 2012(k)(3) the facility is one referred to in section 2012(k)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is currently authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is in a representative sample` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(i)(1)(A) the Secretary must review the facility` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2012(k)(3) the facility is one referred to in section 2012(k)(3)` AND `the facility is currently authorized` AND `the facility is in a representative sample`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The Secretary— (A) shall review a representative sample of currently authorized facilities referred to in section 2012(k)(3)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "a representative sample of currently authorized facilities referred to in section 2012(k)(3)"

-- src:1393 | (B) may carry out similar reviews for currently participating residential drug and alcohol treatment and rehabilitation programs, and group living arrangements for the blind and disabled, referred to in section 2012(k) of this title;
@ref s 2018(i)(1)(B) (src:1393)
GIVEN `s 2012(k) the group living arrangement is one referred to in section 2012(k)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the program or arrangement is currently participating` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(i)(1)(B) the Secretary may review the program or arrangement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2012(k) the group living arrangement is one referred to in section 2012(k)` AND `the program or arrangement is currently participating`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The Secretary— (B) may carry out similar reviews for currently participating residential drug and alcohol treatment and rehabilitation programs, and group living arrangements for the blind and disabled"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for "currently participating" programs and arrangements "referred to in section 2012(k)"

-- src:1394 | (C) shall gather information, and such facilities, programs, and arrangements shall be required to submit information deemed necessary for a full and thorough review; and
@ref s 2018(i)(1)(C) (src:1394)
GIVEN `s 2012(k)(3) the facility is one referred to in section 2012(k)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(k) the group living arrangement is one referred to in section 2012(k)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is deemed necessary for a full and thorough review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(i)(1)(C) the facility, program or arrangement must submit the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 2012(k)(3) the facility is one referred to in section 2012(k)(3)` OR `s 2012(k) the group living arrangement is one referred to in section 2012(k)`) AND `the information is deemed necessary for a full and thorough review`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "such facilities, programs, and arrangements shall be required to submit information deemed necessary for a full and thorough review"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "such facilities, programs, and arrangements" and for "information deemed necessary for a full and thorough review"

-- (i)(1)(D): 18 months after December 20, 2018 is 20 June 2020 (548 days).
-- src:1395 | (D) shall report the results of these reviews to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate not later than 18 months after December 20, 2018, along with recommendations regarding—
@ref s 2018(i)(1)(D), the report was in time (src:1395)
GIVEN `the date the report was submitted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(i)(1)(D) the results of the reviews were reported not later than 18 months after December 20, 2018` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the report was submitted` AT MOST Date 20 6 2020
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "not later than 18 months after December 20, 2018"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall report the results of these reviews ... not later than 18 months after December 20, 2018"

-- (i)(1)(D), the content: the report goes "along with recommendations regarding" two matters.
-- src:1395 | (D) shall report the results of these reviews to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate not later than 18 months after December 20, 2018, along with recommendations regarding—
-- src:1396 | (i) any additional requirements or oversight that would be appropriate for such facilities, programs, and arrangements; and
-- src:1397 | (ii) whether such facilities, programs, and arrangements should continue to be authorized to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2018(i)(1)(D), the recommendations (src:1395-1397)
GIVEN `the report includes recommendations regarding any additional requirements or oversight that would be appropriate for such facilities, programs, and arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes recommendations regarding whether such facilities, programs, and arrangements should continue to be authorized to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(i)(1)(D) the report includes the recommendations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report includes recommendations regarding any additional requirements or oversight that would be appropriate for such facilities, programs, and arrangements` AND `the report includes recommendations regarding whether such facilities, programs, and arrangements should continue to be authorized to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall report the results of these reviews ... along with recommendations regarding— (i) any additional requirements or oversight ...; and (ii) whether such facilities, programs, and arrangements should continue to be authorized"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall report the results of these reviews ... along with recommendations regarding" both matters

DECLARE `s 2018(i)(1)(D) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2018(i)(1)(D) report the results of the reviews to the committees`

-- Time is counted in days from December 20, 2018.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 2018(i)(1)(D) act`
`s 2018(i)(1)(D) the duty to report the results of the reviews` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2018(i)(1)(D) report the results of the reviews to the committees`
    WITHIN 548
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the results of the reviews were not reported within 18 months after December 20, 2018"

-- src:1399 | Nothing in this subsection shall authorize the Secretary to deny any application for continued authorization, any application for authorization, or any request to withdraw the authorization of any such facility, program, or arrangement based on a determination that residents of any such facility or entity are residents of an institution prior to December 31, 2022.
@ref s 2018(i)(2), limitation (src:1399)
GIVEN `the denial is based on a determination that residents of the facility or entity are residents of an institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(i)(2) the subsection authorizes the Secretary to deny the application or request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the denial is based on a determination that residents of the facility or entity are residents of an institution` AND `the date of the determination` LESS THAN Date 31 12 2022
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this subsection shall authorize the Secretary to deny any application ... based on a determination that residents of any such facility or entity are residents of an institution prior to December 31, 2022"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the limit is on a denial "based on a determination that residents ... are residents of an institution prior to December 31, 2022"

§ `s 2018(j) Incentives`

-- src:1402 | In this subsection, the term “eligible incentive food” means—
-- src:1403 | (A) a staple food that is identified for increased consumption, consistent with the most recent dietary recommendations; and
-- src:1404 | (B) a fruit, vegetable, dairy, whole grain, or product thereof.
@ref s 2018(j)(1), eligible incentive food (src:1402-1404)
GIVEN `the food is a staple food that is identified for increased consumption, consistent with the most recent dietary recommendations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the food is a fruit, vegetable, dairy, whole grain, or product thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(j)(1) the food is an eligible incentive food` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the food is a staple food that is identified for increased consumption, consistent with the most recent dietary recommendations` OR `the food is a fruit, vegetable, dairy, whole grain, or product thereof`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "the term eligible incentive food means— (A) a staple food that is identified for increased consumption ...; and (B) a fruit, vegetable, dairy, whole grain, or product thereof"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the term eligible incentive food means"

-- src:1407 | The Secretary shall issue guidance to clarify the process by which an approved retail food store may seek a waiver to offer an incentive, which may be used only for the purchase of an eligible incentive food at the point of purchase, to a household purchasing food with benefits issued under this chapter.
@ref s 2018(j)(2)(A), what the incentive may be used for (src:1407)
GIVEN `the purchase is of an eligible incentive food` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is at the point of purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(j)(2)(A) the incentive may be used for the purchase` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the purchase is of an eligible incentive food` AND `the purchase is at the point of purchase`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an incentive, which may be used only for the purchase of an eligible incentive food at the point of purchase"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only" names what is outside; it does not say that every purchase of an eligible incentive food is allowed

-- src:1409 | The guidance under subparagraph (A) shall establish a process under which an approved retail food store, prior to carrying out an incentive program under this subsection, shall provide to the Secretary information describing the incentive program, including—
-- src:1410 | (i) the types of incentives that will be offered;
-- src:1411 | (ii) the types of foods that will be incentivized for purchase; and
-- src:1412 | (iii) an explanation of how the incentive program intends to support meeting dietary intake goals.
@ref s 2018(j)(2)(B), information before an incentive program (src:1409-1412)
GIVEN `the approved retail food store has provided the Secretary the types of incentives that will be offered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approved retail food store has provided the Secretary the types of foods that will be incentivized for purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approved retail food store has provided the Secretary an explanation of how the incentive program intends to support meeting dietary intake goals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2018(j)(2)(B) the approved retail food store may carry out the incentive program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the approved retail food store has provided the Secretary the types of incentives that will be offered` AND `the approved retail food store has provided the Secretary the types of foods that will be incentivized for purchase` AND `the approved retail food store has provided the Secretary an explanation of how the incentive program intends to support meeting dietary intake goals`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an approved retail food store, prior to carrying out an incentive program under this subsection, shall provide to the Secretary information describing the incentive program, including— (i) the types of incentives that will be offered; (ii) the types of foods that will be incentivized for purchase; and (iii) an explanation of how the incentive program intends to support meeting dietary intake goals"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the information is "including" the three items, and the process the guidance sets may ask for more

-- src:1414 | A waiver granted under this subsection shall not be used to carry out any activity that limits the use of benefits under this chapter or any other Federal nutrition law.
@ref s 2018(j)(3) (src:1414)
GIVEN `the activity limits the use of benefits under this chapter or any other Federal nutrition law` IS A BOOLEAN
