`s 2018(j)(3) the waiver may be used to carry out the activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the activity limits the use of benefits under this chapter or any other Federal nutrition law`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A waiver granted under this subsection shall not be used to carry out any activity that limits the use of benefits under this chapter or any other Federal nutrition law"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "any activity that limits the use of benefits"

-- src:1416 | Guidance provided under this subsection shall not affect any requirements under section 7517 of this title, including the eligibility of a retail food store to participate in a project funded under such section.
@ref s 2018(j)(4) (src:1416)
GIVEN `the requirement is a requirement under section 7517 of this title, including the eligibility of a retail food store to participate in a project funded under such section` IS A BOOLEAN
